<article class="env-definition" id="0B4N">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0B4N">Definition <span data-tag="0B4N">54.8.3</span>.</a> Let $(A, \mathfrak m, \kappa )$ be a local normal Nagata domain of dimension $2$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
We say $A$ <em>defines a rational singularity</em> if for every normal modification $X \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$ we have $H^1(X, \mathcal{O}_ X) = 0$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say that <em>reduction to rational singularities is possible for $A$</em> if the length of the $A$-modules 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  H^1(X, \mathcal{O}_ X)  \]
</div>
<p>
 is bounded for all modifications $X \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$ with $X$ normal. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>